  <title>Edit incoming invoice</title>

  <p>The <gui>Edit Incoming Invoice</gui> window opens from the edit mode of
  <link xref="incoming_invoices_report"/>, <link
  xref="credit_card_statements"/> and <link xref="shipping_history"/>, which
  ask for the administrator password.</p>

  <p>Change the service provider, date, amount, description or attachment,
  and the split over expense accounts, as in <link xref="incoming_invoice"/>.
  Under <gui>Pay</gui>, change the account it was paid <gui>with</gui>, the
  <gui>Cheque number</gui> and the <gui>Transaction description</gui>. Click
  <gui>Save edits</gui>.</p>

  <p>If you replace the attachment you are asked whether to keep the original.
  If the payment has already been reconciled on a bank or card statement, you
  are warned that saving changes that statement's totals.</p>

</page>
